Find which chip (registry without a registry)

~storage/STAR-LUX/posts/post-001.chip
~storage/STAR-LUX/posts/post-002.chip
~storage/STAR-LUX/mail/msg-....chip

// by filename (id in the name)
$path = STORAGE_ROOT . '/' . Space_Slug . '/posts/' . $safeId . '.chip';

// by scanning for a meta field (slow, fine for dozens)
foreach (glob($dir . '/*.chip') as $f) {
  $c = chipParse(file_get_contents($f));
  if (chipGet($c, 'type') === 'post' && chipGet($c, 'id') === $want) {
    // found
  }
}

When you have hundreds, you can add a dumb index later (index.chip listing ids). Not day one.